Replace the third section with reported material not yet drawn from the source â€” the presentation of initial goals mentioned in the source summary, the visibility of Maloney's commit history in the original project, or further development of what Darwin porting actually entails in practice â€” to add at minimum 73 words of sourced content. If the source summary genuinely does not contain additional usable detail beyond what is already in the draft, signal REPORTING_NEEDED rather than padding with inference. Tighten "the maintainers agreed" to an inference marker or drop it in favor of the observable fact that he now leads the project. Tighten the history-page claim to match the source's actual language ("gives credit where it's due") rather than specifying Hubbard's name as a credited party unless the full article confirms it. Fix the tweet to include an emoji and a complete sentence rather than a bare title copy.

