PIPELINE IMPROVEMENT:

The writer model should be guided to use the full extent of available sourced detail before moving into analytical frame sections. When a packet contains a source summary that mentions a linked document (the presentation of initial goals) or a linked artifact (Maloney's commit list), those should be surfaced as specific reportable facts rather than treated as background. The current draft treats the first two sections as reporting and the third as editorial analysis; the genre contract for reported analysis requires every section to carry at least one distinct supported claim. A writer-layer instruction to that effect â€” specifically that a "what this means" section must still be anchored in a new reported fact, not just a restatement of the frame â€” would prevent this class of undercount without requiring a sources replay.

